{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-minor-species-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.74, step 7f. `scale-county-minor-species`: the PM species, the PAH particles, the metals and the dioxins/furans at every exhaust process, NOT aggregated -- the non-aggregated twin of `scale-county-timeagg-year-minor-species`. For source types 21 and 62 on road types 1 and 4 (MOVES adds 2, 3 and 5 for running exhaust's off-network idle), over the county database `inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg.esm`, at `<aggregateBy key=\"Hour\"/>` and `<outputtimestep value=\"Hour\"/>`: July 2020, weekdays, hour 8, with the VMT output on. It selects PM10 and PM2.5 totals (100, 110), organic and elemental carbon (111, 112), sulfate (115), NonECPM (118), aerosol water (119), nitrate and ammonium (35, 36), the PM2.5 elements chloride to iron (51-59), PMOTHR, NCOM, TOM and the residual (121-124) and the PAH particles (23, 68-78, 81-84) at running, start, extended idle, APU and crankcase running, start and extended idle (1, 2, 90, 91, 15, 16, 17), and the metals (60-63, 65-67) and dioxins/furans (130-146) at running exhaust, the only process MOVES associates them with. MOVESOutput is 75,582 rows: 38 pollutants at each of the seven processes (770 rows at running and crankcase running, 154 at start and crankcase start, 50 at extended idle and crankcase extended idle, 41 at APU) and NO metal or dioxin row: the default database has no `sourceTypePolProcess` row for them, so SourceBinDistributionGenerator writes no source-bin distribution and BaseRateGenerator's distance-rate weighting (`SBWeightedDistanceRate`) is empty.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES: SulfatePMCalculator's pmSpeciation outputs beyond organic carbon (nitrate, ammonium, the elements, PMOTHR, NCOM) and its two sums of them (TOM = OC + NCOM, the residual = the residue times one minus their fractions), its crankcase split -- the crankcase processes' PM is the PARENT process's species times `crankcaseEmissionRatio` at the crankcase process -- AirToxicsCalculator's PAH particles from organic carbon at the SAME process (`pahParticleRatio`), crankcase ones included, and the metals' and dioxins' absence.\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 75582, the (pollutant-process, cohort, road type) rows of the one (county, month, hour cell); `n_physicsRow` 21, the two source types' physics rows.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "hotelling-adjustment",
      "crankcase",
      "pm-speciation",
      "air-toxics",
      "running-exhaust",
      "start-exhaust"
    ]
  },
